<title>HONG KONG: HK two-year notes average accepted yield 6.16 pct.</title>
<headline>HK two-year notes average accepted yield 6.16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average accepted yield of two-year 6.12-percent Exchange Fund notes at Monday's tender was 6.16 percent, the Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) said.</p>
<p>This compares with an average accepted yield of 5.58 percent and a coupon of 5.66 percent at the last tender on February 10.</p>
<p>Bids for Monday's HK$500 million issue totalled HK$4.45 billion against HK$2.87 billion at the last tender.</p>
<p>The notes mature on May 13, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
